# CI tools / workflows

- Run cancels and merge methods: AGENTS.md §Coordination (the hooks enforce both). A queued run holds no slot;
  `node tools/ci/queue-depth.mjs` is an informational gauge and nothing holds a push on it.
- Every PR push runs CI: a DRAFT push gets the fast tier only; the `selected`
  browser legs wait for ready (`docs/VERIFICATION.md` §By change). Ready gets the full tier, minus the `selected` legs when another run tested the same
  merge tree on the same base (the unmoved deploy tip) green first try with the same plan, and no run on that tree is red
  (`tools/ci/reuse-draft-selected.mjs`). No label or body line opts in. `= ci none` after a push means no open PR carries the sha (not
  pushed, or no PR yet). A whole browser group: `node tools/ci/remote-group.mjs
  <group>` dispatches on the pushed branch only with Bryce's opt-in (`APEX_GH_OWNER_WRITE=1`, his alone: a dispatch
  on the gh token is recorded as his act); an agent asks with `needs-decision`. Agents never run a browser test
  locally (AGENTS.md rule 5), and `bash-guard.sh` refuses `gh workflow run` and every other gh write. Only the
  orchestrator cancels, re-runs failed jobs or dispatches `ci.yml` / `pages.yml`, through the GitHub MCP, logged
  (skill `steward` §CI; `github-mcp-guard.sh`).
- Sync via `node tools/ci/sync-pr.mjs <branch>` (merge origin, no force); never
  `update_pull_request_branch` from an agent (nothing calls update-branch since
  AUTO-SYNC left on 2026-11-03).
